  "extraction_notes": [
    "PDF SHA-256 verified as c262bbf8a3d5fb65a6fa3d391a1a4402f72c1c92b9707a07665713330782ea35.",
    "The public PDF does not state a document revision or issue date; page and figure citations are retained.",
    "Electrical Characteristics are specified at TJ = 25 \u00b0C unless otherwise noted. Typical Characteristics are specified at TC = 25 \u00b0C unless otherwise noted.",
    "The device is an N-channel MOSFET. Voltage and current values in the scalar fields are positive magnitudes with the datasheet's stated polarity.",
    "Absolute maximum ratings include VDS = 30 V, VGS = \u00b120 V, continuous ID = 30 A at TC = 25 \u00b0C and 22 A at TC = 100 \u00b0C, pulsed IDM = 110 A, EAS = 12 mJ, PD = 24 W at TC = 25 \u00b0C, and TJ/TSTG = -55 to 150 \u00b0C (p. 1).",
    "The BVDSS minimum is 30 V at VGS = 0 V and ID = 250 \u00b5A. IDSS maximum is 1.0 \u00b5A at VGS = 0 V, VDS = 30 V, TJ = 25 \u00b0C. IGSS maximum is \u00b1100 nA at VGS = \u00b120 V and VDS = 0 A (p. 2).",
    "RDS(on) table values preserve both typical and maximum meanings for VGS = 10 V, ID = 10 A and VGS = 4.5 V, ID = 5 A. Datasheet note 3 specifies pulse width \u2264 300 \u00b5s and duty cycle \u2264 0.5%.",
    "Dynamic table values are typical: Ciss = 550 pF, Coss = 105 pF, Crss = 95 pF at the shared condition VDS = 15 V, VGS = 0 V, f = 1 MHz. The values are stored in farads.",
    "Switching table values are typical: td(on) = 5 ns, tr = 8 ns, td(off) = 21 ns, tf = 7 ns with VDS = 30 V, VGS = 10 V, RG = 3.0 ohm, ID = 18 A. Gate-charge values are Qg = 15 nC, Qgs = 4.7 nC, Qgd = 3.6 nC at VDS = 15 V, VGS = 10 V, ID = 10 A (p. 2).",
    "The tabulated body-diode VSD is a maximum of 1.2 V at ISD = 18 A, VGS = 0 V, TJ = 25 \u00b0C. The body-diode curves on p. 3 are typical plots at TJ = 25 \u00b0C and TJ = 150 \u00b0C, with logarithmic current axis.",
    "Transfer, output, on-resistance, body-diode, gate-charge, capacitance, normalized-temperature, and continuous-current curves were digitized from the supplied PDF figures. Curve points are plotted-trace readings, not interpolated table values.",
    "Figure 2 transfer curves are labeled TJ = 25 \u00b0C and TJ = 125 \u00b0C. Figure 4 body-diode curves are labeled TJ = 25 \u00b0C and TJ = 150 \u00b0C. Figure 6 capacitance curves use VGS = 0 V and f = 1 MHz while VDS is swept.",
    "Thermal resistance R\u03b8JC maximum is 5.2 K/W (p. 1). The PDF also provides normalized BVDSS and normalized RDS(on) versus junction temperature and maximum continuous drain current versus case temperature curves on p. 4."
  ],
